<title>LATVIA: British Air starts Latvia flights in March.</title>
<headline>British Air starts Latvia flights in March.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Wednesday that it intended to start flying four times a week to the capital of the Baltic state of Latvia from March 30.</p>
<p>BA is the fifth Western carrier to fly into Latvia after Scandinavian Airlines, Lufthansa, Finnair and  Austrian Airlines.</p>
<p>The company said on a statement the first flight would depart on March 30 from Gatwick to Riga and the first Riga-Gatwick flight would be on March 31.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
